From e3ee706ca62f02a7dd69e8780ab17c66d086e2a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:49:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] P1-printing-module-domain-and-persistence

Printing Module, Phase 1 (Domain + Infrastructure schema only):

- PrintWay, PrintedFace enums (TINYINT, decision Q-06)
- Printer entity: common registry row for both printer families, including Name/Model
  (ERD S6.1, Q-01 - confirmed)
- MaticaPrinterConfiguration: 1:1 Matica-only machine config (ERD S6.2, Q-01)
- RibbonType: global/tenant-agnostic reference table replacing free-text ribbon type (Q-05 - confirmed)
- MaticaProductPrintConfiguration: one row per product, no PrintedFace (Q-02/Q-03/Q-04)
- EvolisProductPrintConfiguration: one row per product, RibbonType FK, PrintedFace retained
  as a descriptive non-key column (Q-02/Q-05 - confirmed)
- PrintImage: upload metadata, tenant-scoped duplicate detection (Q-10); no
  Pending/Attached lifecycle per the locked 'no background cleanup job' decision
- AppDbContext: DbSets + ConfigurePrinterRegistry + ConfigureProductPrintConfigurations
  (indexes, FKs, soft-delete query filters)

CHECK constraints (per explicit confirmation): FontSize > 0 on both
MaticaProductPrintConfigurations and EvolisProductPrintConfigurations only. No other
numeric-range or HEX-format constraints are enforced at the DB level in this module -
full validation (including PrintColor/BackgroundColor HEX format) is deferred entirely
to the Application-layer validator in P2.

Deliberately excludes: EF migration (Designer.cs/ModelSnapshot.cs) - no dotnet SDK or
NuGet access in this sandbox to safely hand-generate the auto-generated snapshot mirror
without compiler verification. Run 'Add-Migration Printing_P1_PrinterRegistry' in Visual
Studio against this Fluent config instead.
